  "contracts": [
    "Literal HTTP/1 200/version/ResponseInfo/body ok primes the same canonical listener; empty oneshot retains a later observation.",
    "The actual canonical handshake is polled first. Pending, published actual AbortHandle, destruction and is_finished precede origin finish.",
    "External cancellation is already complete before stop; actual JoinError task ID is required. Panic resumes unwind with an Arc marker and checks actual typed payload identity.",
    "Canonical JoinSet retains all join ownership. Controller receives AbortHandles, never child JoinHandles or a fabricated JoinError.",
    "Owner outcome, parent/child completion and held TCP closure are captured before backup; client/runtime remain live. Backup cannot make the captured target succeed.",
    "The existing listener, handshake policy, count deadlines and worker wire operations reconstruct exactly to signed base after reversing only the optional observation hooks."
  ],
  "cleanup": "Backup exists before acquisition, retains parents on constructor return and the child on publication. Existing ConnectionPeer/JoinSet protect errors before publication. Explicit backup finitely observes task completion; Drop only requests abort and does not synchronously join.",
